ns":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.09391473245887762,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.19187299370419275,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":6.995,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.040209997,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":26.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.2,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":20.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Shattuck Labs, Inc., a clinical-stage biotechnology company, engages in the development of antibodies for the treatment of inflammatory and immune-mediated diseases in the United States. The company develops SL-325, a death receptor 3 blocking monoclonal antibody, which is in Phase I clinical trial for the treatment of tumor necrosis factor like ligand 1A; and SL-425, a half-life extended version of SL-325, which is under IND-enabling chronic good laboratory practices toxicity study. It is also involved in the development of various preclinical DR3-based bispecific antibodies for the treatment of patients with inflammatory bowel disease or other immune-mediated indications; and TRIM7, an oncology-focused program. The company was incorporated in 2016 and is headquartered in Austin, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Taylor H. Schreiber M.D., Ph.D. | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $876,232 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 40 people. Revenue per employee of $25K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue falling 37%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $175K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 35\u00d7 revenue per employee (elevated relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Shattuck Labs, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $474M market cap on $1M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -944% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $40M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 9.4% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 700% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 5150% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 128% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Shattuck Labs (NASDAQ:STTK) Stock Rating Cut to Sell at Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/08/shattuck-labs-nasdaqsttk-stock-rating-cut-to-sell-at-wall-street-zen.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794132443.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.681,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Shattuck Labs (NASDAQ:STTK) Issues Earnings Results","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/shattuck-labs-nasdaqsttk-issues-earnings-results.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793942811.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","legal"]},{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (STTK) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/22/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_STTK_Price_Events_102926035401_1793260441.html","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793260441.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Shattuck Labs, Inc. (NASDAQ:STTK) Shares Shorted: Short Interest Up 60.8% in September","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.t